Both can present maximum of eight sets to the host machine.
If you have three channel model, you can have upto 21 disks
connected to the controller. But since only eight sets
can be presented, one is forced to create drive groups
and then assign logical drives from those groups using
RAID 0, RAID 1, RAID 0+1 or RAID 5 in order to consume
all those disks. Of course certain number of disks
can be assigned as HSP (hot spare).

And maximum size of a logical drive is 32GB. Hence you
cannot create drive group from say four 9GB drives and
then expect to assign logical drive using RAID 5 as the
size would 36GB, one would have to partition it using only
32GB from the set.

_veli

