Tim,

two ethernet interfaces just to accomodate two protocol stacks is
not quite necessary. Nice for performance perhaps.
AFAIK Multinet had an IP stack for VMS 4.5. MicroVMS has some
components taylored off, but you can always revert to installing regular
VMS 4.5 (provided you have the kit).

If you want to use two devices (lines in NCP jargon) then you need to
have the DECnet routing kit installed and IIRC microVMS has only endnode
capabilities. That does not allow two (ethernet) lines active at the same
time.
You must configure the second device manually. If they're both DEQNA's the
you have a line (and circuit) called XQA-0 . NCP SHO LINE XQA0 CHAR
lists the characteristics (same for the circuit XQA-0).
Do a SET LINE XQA-1 and enter the same values, except STATE, that should be
off.
Similar for circuit XQA-1. Next set the circuit and line states for XQA-0 to
off and
turn XQA-1 on. That should run.
Check vector and IO address settings in SYSGEN:
$ mc sysgen
SYSGEN> config
DEVICE> xqa0                etc

end check for the results.

Hans Vlems

