 reality; the RZ25L-E ones (from a German site) weren't even physically
 correct.  I had to remove Jumper 6 from a block on the right side to get
 the motor to spin.  Then I had a lot of toing-and-froing trying to get DOS
 to accept it.  It wasn't until I had set up a DOS partition (no response),
 low-level format[1] and DOS partition (again no response) that I tried to
 look at the partitions on my Maxtor and received a message that
 triggered a memory.  The Host Controller only works for SCSI IDs 0 and 1!

