Hi all,

I'm getting ready to revive an MV3400 to keep the basement warm this
winter. I've got two questions for the collective: an unknown (to me)
quad height board. probably a tape controller, and a TK70 that isn't
being recognized.

Any help would be appreciated!


Mystery Board:
=============

It looks like it's a tape controller, but I've no clue as to what it
would be hooked up to. I don't see a matching connector on the back
of my Cipher F880 (guess I'll have to get the 11-730 running next ;-).

Here's what you get from doing a SHOW DEV at the >>> prompt:

    [ DSSI devices ]

    UQSSP Tape Controller 0 (774500)
    -?

    UQSSP Tape Controller 1 (760404)
    -?

    [ Ethernet device ]

Here's what you get from doing a SHOW QBUS:

    Scan of Qbus I/O Space
    - 20000104 (760404) = 200D (300) TQK50/TQK70/TU81E/RV20/KFQSA-TAPE
    - 20000106 (760406) = 0A0D
    - 20001940 (774500) = 0000 (260) TQK50/TQK70/TU81E/RV20/KFQSA-TAPE
    - 20001942 (774502) = 827B
    - 20001F40 (777500) = 0020 (004) IPCR

Here's what you can see by inspecting the board itself.

  Name screened on board:         SI - QS 1000
  Serial/model number near same:  6051-7000 -011 (last is sep. tag, like
rev)

  Several Cypress chips/PALs:     CY7C9101-40JC  68 pin PLCC
                                  CY7C910-50JC   44 pin PLCC
                                  CY7C409A-15PC  28 pin DIP (PAL?)

  Three IDC/Berg connectors:      2 x 50 pin
                                  1 x 26 pin


  There are two DIP switch packs, 8 and 10 positions. There is also a
strip
  for 12 jumpers, screened labels run from "TP1" through "TP12".

  The unit came with a slot cover that passes a fat 25 pair cable from
one
  of the 50 pin Berg connectors (P2?), about 10 feet to another 50 pin
Berg.

  Aside from the Cypress chips there is a lot of MSI logic, and a
liberals
  scattering of what I assume are PALs (all narrow 18-22? pin DIPs) with

  paper tags that all start with "6051-xxxx", a few with random-seeming
  version numbers on the second line, e.g. "v.111", "v2a", "v25".


Sick TK70:
=========

This MV3400 includes a TK70 as the primary load device, but it isn't
listed
as a boot device or when I type SHO DEV at the console prompt. I'm not
sure
what this may imply about the controller...

The drive is convinced it has a tape inserted, even though it's empty.
When
it finishes initializing at power up, the green operate-handle light is
lit
solid. The yellow tape-moving light is blinking, and almost never stops.
If
I try to hit the Unload button when it is lit solid, makes no
difference.

The motor does spin fitfully while the yellow light is blinking, and I
think
it's moving in the direction to rewind the tape.

Any clues? I'm not squeamish about taking a screwdriver to the transport
if
you convince me it'll help...



Thanks a bunch for any help on either question!
