towards the E450 in multiple sessions. Single-job performance
varied quite significantly. Given heavy FP-dependency, the Alpha's
came out almost twice as fast on a per-CPU basis and about 1-1.5
the performance on integer code.

I opted for the UP2000, since it was _much_ cheaper than a
Quad E450 and reasonably close to the DS20 on my jobs.
Also, I tend to favor configurations, which provide high performance
with lower CPU-count, because it eases constraints in parallelism.

