I don't think that SCSI priority should matter in your situation, unless you
give the system disk higher priority than your CD writer or a tape that you
want to keep streaming.

Whether a locally attached but full SCSI chain is faster or slower than one
read via MSCP depends on the details, I suppose. The difference in I/O
performance between a VAX and an Alpha should be much lower than the
difference in CPU performance for comparable I/O systems.

	Jan



