>I have a problem on a machine DEC Alpha equips with True Unix version
>4.0F. The problem relates to the creation of process defunct during the
>use of a SGBD0 (Versant ODBMS not to quote it).
>They are the processes of the server which detruise badly, for a reason
>which is unknown for me and I seek tracks.
>
>The problem is that precisely the process father is itself in state
>which apparently does not allow him to treat the end of his/her son
>(what causes the passage completely normally has the state of
>zombie). Moreover it cannot be detruit (I seek has to know why) and
>his/her father is the process init (what is facheux). The reboot thus
>seems inevitable. The process father east blocks after a call has the
>primitive sigprocmask. A idee? Other question: is not it not possible
>to purge the table of the processes (so as to eliminate the zombies)
>without rebooter?

If you kill the parent process, all the zombies will be inherited by
"init", which will reap them.  If the parent process doesn't reap its
children properly, that's the only way to purge them without rebooting.

This should be explained in the Unix FAQ, which can be found at
www.faqs.org.  It has an extensive section on zombies.

