:But at least for my situation this statement is false. 

  SCSI can be (is) quite phase-of-the-moon dependent -- I have seen 
  various correct SCSI configurations that simply do not work, or that
  are flakey at best.  

  When a SCSI bus gets too long or when various components of differing 
  SCSI-x support are mixed together, strange and beautiful things can 
  happen -- hopefully, the transfers are slowed and the bus does not 
  become unstable.  This is not always the case, however.

