>> Hi there :-) I am very new to VAX/VMS.  I have recently got A Vaxstation
>> 3100 with what I believe to be 16 MB RAM, the unit came with A 104MB drive
>> in it which I am replacing with A 1 gig drive, what I would like to know is
>> that if I install A CD-ROM that reads in 512 byte blocks, (There is no
>> operating system on the drive), What must I do in order to accsess the
>> CD-ROM with OpenVMS on it - Do I have to type any commands? If so what are
>> they? does the unit simply attempt to boot from the CD-ROM on its own?
>> 
>Easy ;-) Connect your CD-ROM to the SCSI-bus (Toshiba or Pioneer
>are fine) Switch on your VAX.
>
>The console prompt ">>>" appears if system is not bootable.
>
>enter "SHOW DEVICE" and you will see your SCSI-devices "DKAxyy"
>where x is the devices scsi-id.
>
>Insert your OpenVMS-CD into the drive and enter "BOOT DKAxyy"
>(as seen from "SHOW DEVICE") to boot from your CD.
>
>That's all.
>
