In article <3A101BEC.95888D33@lbl.gov>, Tobias Funk <funk@lbl.gov> writes:

> We are using a alpha machine with VMS 6.2. I am writing a fortran
> program and trying to use a system command. I know that you can do this
> wit fortran under unix with the following command:
> value=system("command"). Is there something comparable under VMS?

        Yes, you probably want LIB$SPAWN.   Look  it  up in the Run-time
    Library  reference  manual,  or  the online help as  HELP  RTL  LIB$
    LIB$SPAWN.  There are a number of differences between unix and  VMS,
    so  the  above  may  or  may not work as you expect.  But that's the
    starting point.

        Note that VMS questions are usually better asked on comp.os.vms.

