You will want to look at the individual link counters for the links
that are going down (or are _all_ links going down simultaneously?).  A
MUXserver 380 supports up to 8 links, two at up to 64Kbps, and 6 at up
to 19.2Kbps,.

Note that the total bandwidth this unit can support is actually LOWER
than the sum of the bandwidth of its ports; if I recall correctly the
limit is 128Kbps.  If you are running the two high-speed ports at
64Kbps each, thats all it can handle.  If at 56Kbps each (more common
in North America), then running even one slow line at 19.2K is still
pushing you over the limit.  When the maximum bandwidth is exceeded,
you can get flaky problems, random drops, one or all links 'freezing'
(where they claim to still be up but you cannot query the remote end
of the link)

Other possible problems; excessive latency on the network link between 
the MS380 and the LAT host; network faults on the LAN side, LAN controller
problem on the LAT host, or an actual hardware problem on the MS380.  It
would be worth making sure you are running the latest software for the
box (I'm sorry, I don;t have the information available here).

Rich Jordan
rjordan@mcs.net




