A VAX 6310 is rated at 3.8 VUPS. The list is as follows:

6200 2.8
6300 3.8
6400 8
6500 24

We still have a couple of 6300's and 6400's in running condition. They're
not doing serious
work anymore (we have an 8550 for that ;-).
The good news is that these machines seem to run forever. We stopped paying
for maintenance
years ago and it was decided to throw them out as soon as they fail. Well,
ahum, they just happened
not to fail....
The bad news is that the cabinets are big and heavy and the machines run on
three phase power
(at least ours do).
As for central heating, they're fine. Come to think of it, one VAX 6xxx per
floor and an HSC50
in the cellar and the attic will give you a pretty good CI cluster as well
as heating!

Hans Vlems

