Chris Scheers wrote:
> Actually, on the units I converted, I did not need to change the ROMs.
> As far as I can tell, the only difference in the -38 ROM is that it
> identifies itself as a -B as opposed to -A.  VMS can't tell the
> difference between the two units.

I believe that you are correct in that you do not need
to change the ROMs (assuming you don't mind an inconsistent
console identification).

I am fairly certain, however, that there is at least one
place where OpenVMS *could* tell the difference and that
is when it is determining the delay value used for short
timed loops in a driver macro. Whether OpenVMS chooses
to actually note this difference or not I cannot remember.

Antonio

