> but nothing seems to work. I need to know
> the following things:
> 
> Which of the serial ports on the Alphastation will be
> used by SRM when it defaults to the serial console
> (after not detected a keyboard)?

I usually use the top one on an AlphaStation 200. This is called port A
or 1, depending on where you look. I think there might be some
circumstances where the other port can be used, but I have never done
that.

> What are the protocol settings that will be used (I am
> currently using 9600 buad, no parity, 8 data bits, and
> 1 stop bit)?

That should work.

> Do I need a straight through serial cable, or a
> null-modem cable (I can't remember if PCs are wired
> like terminals or like real computers and I don't know
> if the Alphastation is wired like a PC -- though I
> suspect it is)?

You will need a cross-over (null modem) cable. The AlphaStation serial
ports are essentially PC serial ports. So, if you have two of the same
kind of ports talking to each other, you have to cross the wires.
 
> Do I need to do anything in SRM before this will work?

>>> set console serial

although if there is no keyboard plugged in, I think this happens
automatically.

