The DECsystem 5400 is a 16MIPS MIPS box :-)
The CPU Module set is a KN210, uses MS650-BA memory
and has a Qbus. It can support RA and RF drives.
You could certainly add a KZQSA to get SCSI support
(and I believe it would work with Ultrix).

It's fairly easy to create "mongrels" with these
systems (I don't recall if this one is BA200
or BA430 based) but I don't think VAX 4000 is
a possibility since that needs a BA440 and the 
special CPU/memory slots which a KN210 would not
be at all happy about.


