Originator: rjordan@mars.mcs.net (Richard Jordan)

This is from the Oct-Dec 1989 SOC listing for a VAXstation 3520.

12 slots, numbered 1-12 with 10 through 12 being Qbus reserved slots.

Slot 1 - 16 plane graphics module (optional)
Slot 2 - 8 plane graphics module (mandatory)
Slot 3 - Graphics module (mandatory)
Slot 4 - Input/Output (mandatory)
Slot 5 - Memory (optional)
Slot 6 - Memory or CPU module (optional)
Slot 7 - CPU module (mandatory)
Slot 8 - Memory (8 or 16MB) (mandatory)
Slot 9 - Memory or tape kit (optional) (VS60B-AA tape kit, optional)
Slot 10 - Qbus reserved/tape kit second card (VS60B-AA) (optional)
Slot 11 - Qbus reserved
Slot 12 - Qbus reserved

A 3540 would have its second dual CPU module in slot 6, mandatory.
Since that CPU goes in one of 4 memory-capable slots, maximum
RAM is reduced to 48MB.  


The system is listed as supporting OpenVMS and Ultrix-32,  Maximum of
64MB RAM, 1280x1024 display on a 2k by 2k image buffer, 8 plane base
or 24 plane optional graphics, double buffered, 24-bit Zbuffer, etc.

Memory modules: MS60-AA (8MB, ECC) and MS60-BA (16MB, ECC)

Graphics option is VCB03-AA, 16 plane true color dedicated slot

Mass storage listed is RZ55A-SA, 332MB, max of 4 (3 with tape)

CPU option is KA60-AA, dual CPU to upgrade to 3540

Tape storage kit VS60B-AA, takes 1 memory slot, 1 Qbus slot

Ultrix-32 "Single User Kit", DECwindows/doc is QA-0JQAA-H5

There is a note that "when the Qbus adapter kit is available, you
can substitute the Qbus adapter kit for the TKQ70/TK70 tape"

Hope this is of some help...

Rich Jordan
rjordan@mcs.net




