> Bernd Eckstein wrote:
> > Can you tell more about the crystal to change and this Jumper ?
> > My 3130 waits for it... ;-)
> 
> The VAXstation 3100 Model 30 was enhanced to produce a
> VAXstation 3100 Model 38 (or 40 vs 48 if you have the
> bigger box). At the time the (slower) VAXstation 3100
> Model 30 was still being sold. To reduce costs, the
> VAXstation 3100 Model 30 mainboard was replaced with the
> VAXstation 3100 Model 38 motherboard but with a slower
> crystal and the Model 30 ROMs.
> 
> So if you have a later Model 30 you can upgrade the
> crystal and swap the ROMs and you buy yourself 30%
> extra performance. The instructions are kicking
> around on the net somewhere.
> 
> I don't have the relevant 2-5-2 numbers handy for
> you to identify whether you have a "newer" Model 30
> board or not the relevant numbers have been posted
> in the past. Find the number for the VAXstation 3100
> Model 38 and if yours is the same except the last two
> digits are -02 instead of -01 (or a similar change)
> then you are in with a chance.
> 
> Personally, I'd bet that you can get a VS3100-38 cheaper
> from the net than it will cost you in solder and
> ROMs :-)

Actually, on the units I converted, I did not need to change the ROMs. 
As far as I can tell, the only difference in the -38 ROM is that it
identifies itself as a -B as opposed to -A.  VMS can't tell the
difference between the two units.

