>>   I want to read a file at True64 UNIX, which was written at Open 
>> VMS/AXP using Fortran "unformatted write" statement.  But the following 
>> errors occurs during the unformatted read at True64 UNIX, DEC Fortran.
>> 
>>     forrtl: severe (24): end-of-file during read, unit 1, file testi.d
>>           
>>     forrtl: severe (67): input statement requires too much data, unit 1, 
>>     file testi.d    or
>> 
>>   What I did is as follows:
>> 
>>   (1) Write a file using  Fortran "unformatted write" on VMS. (write.f)
>>       (OpenVMS V6.2-1H3, DIGITAL Fortran 77 X7.1-156, UCX 4.2 ECO 2)
>> 
>>   (2) Binary ftp the file testi.d from Open VMS/AXP to True64 UNIX
>> 
>>   (3) Read the file using Fortran "unformatted read" on True64 UNIX (read.f)
>>       (OSF1 V4.0 1229 alpha, DIGITAL Fortran 77 V5.2-171-428BH)
>> 
>>    Then the read error occurs with the error messages above. 
>> 
>>    Is there any special method to transfer or convert file written by 
>> "unformatted write" on Open VMS/AXP Fortran to True64 UNIX System ?  
>> Thanks for the information.

  I got an answer from telephon support center of Compaq Japan just now.
The suggested method is as follows:

(1) Convet a file to fix record format at the OPEN/VMS using the
    following command:

       $ set file /attr=(rfm=fix,lrl=512) testi.d

(2) Copy the file from VMS to True64 UNIX via binary-mode FTP

(3) At True64 Unix, Open the file with the special option
     RECORDTYPE='segmented' 
    (this option seems to be special to the True64 DEC Frortan)

      open(1,file='testi.d',status='old',form='UNFORMATTED',
     1     RECORDTYPE='segmented')

Then it worked.  Thanks for the information and suggestions.

			Takashi Ichihara (ichihara @ riken.go.jp)


