support was an issue so I went ahead and installed Tru64 v5.1 on my DEC
3000/300LX with 64M ram. It appears to be working fine - not real fast
but much less painful than Solaris 7 on a Sparc2 (a "supported"
configuration). As far as Turbochannel card support goes, I can't tell.
I ran the built in framebuffer for installation but the machine will be
headless most of the time with a remote display using VNC.

BTW, preliminary benchmarking of the 3000/300 with seti@home shows some
interesting results. Running NetBSD, one seti job took 77 hours. With
Tru64, one job takes 43 hours. This is based on single run comparisons,
YMMV.





