Ben Jirou <bluesky6@ix.netcom.com> writes:
> What are the differences between them? For example, I have see
> MicroVax 3100, VaxServer 3100 and VaxStation 3100.

  For the original 3100's, the VAXserver and VAXstation used the same
hardware, and the server/station difference was based on whether there
was a LK keyboard plugged into it. Even the VAXservers had bitonal
graphics on the mainboard, and nothing prevented you from putting a
higher-end graphics card in the VAXserver.

  The Models 3x/4x differed only in the size of the cabinet (4x was
bigger) and the difference between the Models x0/x8 was the CPU speed.
It was possible to speed up a Model x0 by changing the crystal and a
jumper in many (but not all) cases. It still ID'd itself as a x0 un-
less you changed the boot ROMs, in which case it would correctly re-
port itself as an x8.

  The MicroVAX 3100's were somewhat later, somewhat faster boxes with
different innards than the VAXstation/VAXserver 3100's. Some of the
MicroVAX 3100's received different boot ROMs and were sold as Info-
Servers.

  So, 2 basic designs, 4 products.

