Try H-FREQ and H-PHAS for the horizontal and V-SIZE and V-POS for the
vertical adjustment. The labels are stamped into the metal shielding.
You can see tham after you take the outer plastic shell off. The
controls are along the lower edges of the case. Beware of high voltages
inside the case. Also, it is probably possible to damage a fixed freq.
monitor by jacking around with the frequency controls too much. Don't
try this at home unless you can accept the risks.

The VRT19-DA has a diagram stuck to the shielding that shows which
controls work and which are not connected.
I don't know if the HA model has the diagram.

