Hello --

I don't have a TRU64 UNIX to test this myself, but in no particular order:

1) Did you try the ftp transfer in text (vs. binary) mode?
2) Are you sure the 'format' of the TRU64 unformatted data files is the same
as on VMS?  On VMS, each unformatted record is a 'logical record', which is
implemented as a series of one or more variable length records with a
two-byte header (values 00 - 03) that dictates which 'part' of a 'logical'
record it is -- first record, last record, 'middle record', and only record.
This allows the unformatted records to be of arbitrary length.  I am
uncertain of the TRU64 implementation.

Perhaps Steve Lionel of COMPAQ will be able to clear this up.

Ken Randell

